From 973689238f1f931553616ed39d8e58b84ea020d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Walters <jackwalterswork@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:55:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] git_ui: Draw the pictures in a merge request's
 description

A description's pictures showed only as their link text. GitLab writes a
link to a file uploaded to the project as /uploads/<secret>/<name>, which
is no address by itself and needs the user's login to fetch, so the
markdown could not load it. Each such picture is now fetched once through
glab when the merge request loads, kept in the review cache for a month,
and drawn from its file as it arrives, in a table cell or an img tag
alike. A picture elsewhere on the web is loaded from its address. A video
keeps its link text, since it cannot be drawn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
